<title>UK: Iran tenders to buy white, raw sugar - traders.</title>
<headline>Iran tenders to buy white, raw sugar - traders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran's Government Trading Corporation (GTC) tendered on Monday to buy 14,000 tonnes of white sugar and 30,000 tonnes of raws, traders said.</p>
<p>The shipment period was March for the whites and March 15/April 15 for the raws, they said. The tender's deadline was 1500 GMT.</p>
<p>Last month a senior Iranian delegation said Iran would need to buy around 600,000 tonnes of sugar in 1997, some of which could come from Turkey.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
